L4-E5: SOURCE CONTROL FOR BOARD A'S CHARGER ON THE ORED BUS (l4e5_source_control.py, MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN:
nothing bought, built, powered or measured; no generator, registry, rendered page or HW-FW-CONTRACT.md in the tree edited.
Basis per figure: MAKER (document, page), NETLIST, MODELED (l4e_replay.py's functions), INFERRED (method stated),
ASSUMPTION; INCONCLUSIVE where no held document gives the figure.

0. REPRODUCTIONS BEFORE ANY RESULT
   0a l4e4_limits.py re-run in a child process reproduces l4e4_limits.out byte for byte: yes
   0b r11_dep.py re-run in a child process reproduces r11_dep.out byte for byte: yes
   0c l4e4_limits.compute() run here renders l4e4_limits.out byte for byte: yes
   0d l4e_replay.main() run here (locals captured by l4e4_limits.run_main_captured) prints l4e_replay.out byte for byte: yes
   and its corrected A2 rows re-run by this script give the printed unserved figures: 100 W screening 286.3 / 516.5 Wh,
   candidate panel 1196.1 / 1950.7 Wh (48 / 72 h, the worse start)

1. WHAT THE BOARDS CARRY (NETLIST, read from the committed netlists)
   - E: VIN_MON = R40 100k over R41 10k, U10 pin 39
   - E: DCIN_PGD = U6 (LM5069) pin 8 to U10 pin 15, R25 10k to +3V3_E6
   - E: U6 VIN pin 2 on DC_P, SENSE pin 1 on HS_S, OUT pin 9 on DC_HS
   - E: Q7 the hot-swap pass FET, source pins 1-3 on DC_HS, drain pin 5 on HS_S
   - E: L2 passes DC_HS (pad 1) to VIN_RAW (pad 3)
   - E: R19 10 mOhm between DC_P and HS_S
   - E: the vehicle's ideal diode U3 (LM74700) DC_F to DC_P, the tracker's U4 TRK_OUT to VIN_RAW
   - E: LT8705A U5 pins 25 to 28 (SRVO_FBIN, SRVO_IIN, SRVO_IOUT, SRVO_FBOUT) unconnected
   - E: U10 pins 31, 32 (GPIO20, 21) and 41 (GPIO29, ADC3) unconnected
   - E: the tracker's FBOUT divider R10 115k over R11 10.0k
   - A: U3 (BQ25731) pin 6 ILIM_HIZ on CHG_ILIM, R19 16.5k from REGN, R20 34.8k to GND, Q6 drain
   - A: U3 pin 1 (VBUS) on VBUS20
   - A: FE_PGOOD on U27 pin 20, CHRG_OK on U27 pin 13, U27 INT on EXP_INT
   - A: no IC pin on VIN_RAW, FE_UVS or FE_RUN reaches a controller (no reading of VIN_RAW on board A)
   board A's VIN_RAW members: C11, C12, D19, D2, J_VR1, J_VR2, J_VR3, J_VR4, Q2, R14, R195, R196, R200, TP13
   board E's VIN_RAW members: C7, C8, D2, L2, P_VR, Q2, R27, R40, TP3, U4
   FW-A16 as written (HW-FW-CONTRACT.md): IIN_HOST at or below 0.80 x 4.80 A x 0.93 x VIN_RAW / 20.7 V = 0.172522 A/V x VIN_RAW;
   its own figures 1.55 / 2.07 / 4.14 A at 9 / 12 / 24 V reproduced; O-33: about 54 W against the tracker's 93 W
   FW-E04 reports VIN_MON over USB every 1 s; board E's USB goes to board B's bank 3, the panel controller (the charger's
   only host, on the kit bus) is a USB device on bank 1 (FW-C12): VIN_RAW reaches the charger's host only through a running
   compute module's bridge. Board A has no reading of VIN_RAW at all.
   REQ-015 (l3r2.yaml): "A 9 to 36 V vehicle and shore input runs the kit and charges the pack"
   the front end's restart guard U34 (gen_sch_a.py): UV falling 7.86 / 8.08 / 8.31 V; a dip under 8 V interrupts charging for
   1.0 to 2.5 s; the vehicle entry's LM5069 limits at 4.85 to 6.15 A (4.80 A with R19's 1 %); VIN_RAW's clamp 64.5 V

2. WHY THE SOURCES CANNOT BE TOLD APART, AND HOW FAST THE BUS COLLAPSES
   - VIN_MON's value: REQ-015 admits every voltage from 9 to 36 V, the tracker's whole output range included (as drawn
     14.62 / 15.09 / 15.56 V: FBOUT 1.191 / 1.207 / 1.222 V, MAKER 8705af p.4, every grade; R10 and R11 at 1 %): no voltage band is
     the tracker's alone (INFERRED).
   - DCIN_PGD: the LM5069 raises PGD when OUT is within 1.25 V of SENSE (MAKER SNVS452G p.3 and p.12, 8.3.6). Q7's source
     is on DC_HS and its drain on HS_S, so the tracker feeds DC_P back through Q7's body diode whenever it holds VIN_RAW over
     the 9 V UVLO; the LM5069 then starts with OUT above SENSE and PGD reads high with no vehicle connected (INFERRED from
     the netlist and the maker's PGD rule). The vehicle's own ideal diode U3 blocks the back-feed at DC_F (MAKER SNOSD17G
     p.12), so nothing on board E sees whether a vehicle is plugged in while the tracker holds the bus.
   - The LT8705A's SRVO_FBIN and SRVO_FBOUT (pins 25 and 28, open drain, pulled low while the input or output voltage loop
     is active; MAKER 8705af p.11 and p.19; SRVO_FBIN asserts 56 / 72 / 89 mV above FBIN's regulation, p.4) would tell
     'the panel limits' from 'the tracker regulates'; both are unconnected (NETLIST).
   - The collapse: VIN_RAW and TRK_OUT hold 129 uF nominal (NETLIST: A C11 10u, A C12 10u, E C7 1u, E C8 10u, E C24 39u, E C25 39u, E C26 10u, E C27 10u).
     From the tracker's 15.09 V to the latch's highest 8.31 V that is 10.23 mJ, so a constant-power deficit empties it in
     10.2 ms at 1 W, 3.4 ms at 3 W, 1.0 ms at 10 W (INFERRED: energy over deficit; nominal estimates pending evidence of the effective capacitance).
   - The vehicle entry: C5 100 nF on TIMER (NETLIST) with VTMRH 3.76 / 4 / 4.16 V and 51 / 85 / 120 uA (MAKER SNVS452G p.6) gives a
     fault timeout of 3.13 / 4.71 / 8.16 ms before Q7 turns off (INFERRED, C x V / I).
   - FW-E04's 1 s period is 319 times the entry's shortest fault timeout: no firmware rule fed by VIN_MON can act inside a
     source step. Steady state and transients are therefore separate acceptances, as A-2 asks.

3. THE CANDIDATES' PER-SOURCE ENVELOPES (vehicle and shore at the entry's FW-A16 basis 4.80 A, the front end at 0.93 and
   VBUS20 at its 20.7 V maximum; U3's and the pin's maxima in board current with R16 at its low corner, L4-E4's rules;
   VBUS20's other loads 0.079094 A)
   VIN_RAW | FW-A16 line | (a) register, FE input | (b) register, FE input | H pin V | pin target lo/hi | H effective max | H FE input
     9.0 V |  1.553 A    | 1.55 A, 4.333 A ( 90.3 %) | 1.55 A, 4.333 A ( 90.3 %) | 1.621 V | 1.337 / 1.768 A | 1.793 A | 4.629 A ( 96.4 %)
    12.0 V |  2.070 A    | 2.05 A, 4.190 A ( 87.3 %) | 2.05 A, 4.190 A ( 87.3 %) | 1.828 V | 1.850 / 2.291 A | 2.323 A | 4.455 A ( 92.8 %)
    24.0 V |  4.141 A    | 4.10 A, 4.025 A ( 83.9 %) | 4.10 A, 4.025 A ( 83.9 %) | 2.656 V | 3.899 / 4.382 A | 4.443 A | 4.194 A ( 87.4 %)
    36.0 V |  6.211 A    | 6.20 A, 4.033 A ( 84.0 %) | 4.70 A, 3.069 A ( 63.9 %) | 3.484 V | 5.949 / 6.473 A | 4.884 A | 3.069 A ( 63.9 %)
   (a)'s register passes L4-E4's 4.70 A from 27.6 V and reaches 6.20 A at 36 V (U3's clamp 6.35 A, MAKER SLUSE66A p.25).
   The hardware line (H): V(ILIM_HIZ) = 1 V + 40 x IDPM x RAC (MAKER SLUSE66A p.6), the lower of the pin and IIN_HOST
   governs (p.6, p.26 9.3.6), the pin read continuously (p.6). Its line: 1.000 V + 0.069009 V/V x VIN_RAW at R16 10 mOhm.
   The pin's accuracy is printed only for a 5 mOhm RAC: +-0.400 A at every row (2.6 V 7.6/8.0/8.4 A, 2.2 V 5.6/6.0/6.4 A, 1.6 V 2.6/3.0/3.4 A, 1.2 V 0.6/1.0/1.4 A; p.10); at R16's 10 mOhm
   INFERRED +-0.200 A (the same error at the pin); INCONCLUSIVE until measured. The network's own tolerance +-1 % (ASSUMPTION).
   H's highest front-end input current over 9 to 36 V: 4.629 A at 9.0 V, 96.4 % of 4.80 A, under the entry's 4.85 A minimum;
   it reaches 4.80 A only if the front end's efficiency at 9 V falls to 0.897 (C-8: undocumented).
   The pin stays inside its range: 3.509 V at 36 V, 5.496 V at the clamp's 64.5 V (recommended 6.5 V, absolute 7 V, p.8);
   it disables itself above 4.0 V (p.80) only above 43.5 V of VIN_RAW, outside service, where IIN_HOST still holds.
   Solar under (a): the tracker's nominal 15.09 V reads as 2.60 A, 53.9 W at 20.7 V (O-33); under H1 the same line in
   hardware, 2.296 A at the tracker's lowest ceiling. H2 raises the tracker's ceiling so the line's MINIMUM covers the window:
   the window's 4.517 A at the lowest bus (l4e_replay.out 8, MODELED; L4-E4's need) needs the line at 4.828 A, VIN_RAW 27.98 V;
   R10 at least 229 k, so E96 232 k: ceiling 28.28 / 29.21 / 30.15 V (INFERRED, the sheet's FBOUT rows, R10 and R11 at 1 %),
   inside REQ-015's 36 V. TRK_OUT's parts at that ceiling's maximum: C24 39u 35V Panasonic 35SVPF39M polymer at 86 % of its 35 V; C25 39u 35V Panasonic 35SVPF39M polymer at 86 % of its 35 V; C26 10u 25V at 121 % of its 25 V; C27 10u 25V at 121 % of its 25 V
   Low light under H1 and H2: the bus settles below the latch, and the front end restarts, when the power at VBUS20 is under
   36.2 W (nominal 31.3 W); under H1 to H3 it settles below 12 V under 49.7 W (nominal 44.5 W) (INFERRED: the pin's band at 8.31 V and 12 V).
   H3 adds a knee under REQ-015's 9 V floor: the pin falls from the line at 9.00 V to 1 V (no current) at 8.75 V (SESSION)
   and on down. The pin's thresholds are TI's, the network's +-0.5 % (ASSUMPTION) carried through each (nominal, low to high):
     zero-current target, the pin at 1.0 V (p.6's equation at IDPM 0): VIN_RAW 8.750 V (8.706 to 8.794 V)
     HIZ entry, the pin falling to 0.4 V (p.17 VHIZ_HIGH; p.6 'below 0.4 V'): VIN_RAW 8.508 V (8.466 to 8.551 V)
     HIZ exit, the pin rising to 0.8 V (p.17 VHIZ_LO; p.6 'above 0.8 V'; p.27): VIN_RAW 8.669 V (8.626 to 8.713 V)
     the printed regulation range starting at 1.15 V on the pin (p.10): VIN_RAW 8.810 V (8.766 to 8.854 V)
   So U3 is certainly in HIZ below 8.466 V of VIN_RAW, 0.156 V above the latch's highest, and out of HIZ (with EN_HIZ = 0,
   REG0x35 bit 7, reset 0b, p.64; p.27) above 8.713 V; between them the state depends on the sweep's direction and the
   comparator's unprinted spread. Out of HIZ is not proven conversion: TI specifies regulation by the pin only from 1.15 V on
   the pin (p.10), VIN_RAW 8.854 V at the band's top; from HIZ release to there the switching and the input current are
   recorded, not asserted (V-A09).
   The pin along the knee: 0.130 V at 8.400 V, 0.294 V at 8.466 V, 0.399 V at 8.508 V, 0.627 V at 8.600 V, 0.799 V at 8.669 V, 0.876 V at 8.700 V, 0.908 V at 8.713 V, 1.000 V at 8.750 V, 1.149 V at 8.810 V, 1.621 V at 9.000 V.
   At the 9 V floor U3 still gets at least 1.068 A (REQ-015's "charges"). TI's +-0.4 A row is the current loop's accuracy,
   not the HIZ comparator's, so it is not carried into the HIZ thresholds.
   The knee's slope at the pin is 2.484 V/V against the line's 0.0690 V/V: it needs a gain stage, not a divider (OWED).
   H3's settle point on the solar hold (the stage at FBIN, the pin taking what the panel gives; VBUS20 nominal 20.000 V,
   the extremes over the pin's band and VBUS20 19.146 to 20.7 V):
      86.5 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 24.61 V nominal (22.06 V to 27.52 V), U3 up to 4.439 A
      60.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 16.93 V nominal (14.81 V to 19.30 V), U3 up to 3.055 A
      50.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 14.03 V nominal (12.08 V to 16.20 V), U3 up to 2.532 A
      40.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 11.13 V nominal (9.34 V to 13.10 V), U3 up to 2.010 A
      30.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 8.98 V nominal (8.93 V to 10.00 V), U3 up to 1.488 A
      20.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 8.90 V nominal (8.86 V to 8.94 V), U3 up to 0.966 A
      10.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 8.82 V nominal (8.78 V to 8.86 V), U3 up to 0.443 A
       5.0 W at VBUS20: VIN_RAW 8.78 V nominal (HIZ cycling to 8.81 V), U3 up to 0.182 A
   Under 5.8 W at VBUS20 the pin's own error alone can ask more than the stage gives: U3 cycles in and out of HIZ
   above the latch (INFERRED), and the front end never restarts.
   B3 of the check: a source-blind line held at H3's 9 V target up to 12 V, then rising with H3's slope (the knee kept).
   For ANY source-blind line the solar power that settles the bus at 12 V is the charge power the line admits from a 12 V
   source (the same pin target at the same VIN_RAW; INFERRED). H3: 49.720 W; the example: 38.748 W. At 40 W the example's
   lowest settle is 12.342 V against H3's 9.342 V. Its price: at 12 V 1.55 A (31.1 W at VBUS20 nominal) against H3's 2.07 A (41.4 W),
   at 24 V 3.62 A against 4.14 A, against the profile's 42.8 W at the pack terminals; and its window needs the tracker's ceiling
   at 30.98 V at the least (R10 261 k: 31.66 / 32.71 / 33.76 V), the 35 V polymer then at 96 %. Its front end's highest input 4.629 A.
   Rejected variant, an offset through zero at 8.4 V (slope 0.22503 A/V bounded at 36 V): 9 V 0.14 A against 1.55 A, 12 V 0.81 A against 2.07 A, 24 V 3.51 A against 4.14 A; the tracker would sit at 29.9 V.

