5. THE DECISION (engineering, the session's; the reasons are on the page)
   H3: U3's input-current limit made a function of VIN_RAW in hardware, on its own ILIM_HIZ pin: FW-A16's line from REQ-015's
   9 V floor up, a knee into HIZ below it; the tracker's output ceiling raised (R10 232 k) so the line admits the window;
   firmware holds IIN_HOST at L4-E4's 4.70 A ceiling and no longer reads VIN_RAW for control.

6. THE CHOSEN RULE'S CONTRACT VALUES
   values U3's IIN_HOST ever holds under H3: at POR, RSNS_RAC = 1b, board current (the larger annotation) 3.25 A; after every adapter removal (one-time reset, p.26, p.80) 3.25 A; firmware ceiling (FW-A16 restated) 4.70 A; highest 4.70 A (code 94, 0x5E00)
   the pin's line crosses IIN_HOST at 27.24 V; between 26.50 and 27.24 V the pin governs and its maximum passes U3's own 4.817 A
   POR, IIN_HOST 2000h (p.80 heading): 3.20 A in the 5 mOhm table's terms (Table 9-50, pp.80 and 81; its reset bits read 0x20), 1.600 A of
   board current at RSNS_RAC = 1b over R16 (INFERRED); recorded raw by V-A09, kept apart from the removal reset
   POR, IIN_HOST 4100h (p.80 figure): 6.50 A in the 5 mOhm table's terms (Table 9-50, pp.80 and 81; its reset bits read 0x20), 3.250 A of
   board current at RSNS_RAC = 1b over R16 (INFERRED); recorded raw by V-A09, kept apart from the removal reset
   stale or missing VIN_MON (older than 3 s): no setting changes; the line is hardware. Diagnostic only: a fresh VIN_MON
   with the charger's input reading over the pin's band by 0.3 A in three readings falls back to FW-A16's old rule.
   V-A10's values: the trip at 12 V 2.623 A of board current; with the pin lifted above 4.0 V U3 can reach 4.884 A, over it;
   the fallback's registers 9 V 1.55 A, 12 V 2.05 A, 24 V 4.10 A, 36 V 4.70 A; stale 1.55 A; the highest 4.70 A, at or under 4.70 A

7. THE CONSEQUENCE FOR L4-E4 (its own functions, from compute() above)
   L4-E4's setting 4.70 A, U3's maximum 4.817 A, through R11 4.964 A; R11 8 mOhm, C-1 0.3803 mOhm at 25 C. Its margins:
      -20.0 C: R11 alone +0.309 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.218 A, C-1's full taps +0.097 A
       25.0 C: R11 alone +0.317 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.207 A, C-1's full taps +0.064 A
       62.1 C: R11 alone +0.307 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.183 A, C-1's full taps +0.023 A
   H3 writes nothing above 4.70 A, so every register path holds. The pin path just under the crossover: at most 5.016 A in
   board current, 5.095 A through R11 (INFERRED with the pin's +-0.200 A and the network's 1 %):
      -20.0 C: R11 alone +0.178 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.087 A, C-1's full taps -0.034 A
       25.0 C: R11 alone +0.185 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.076 A, C-1's full taps -0.067 A
       62.1 C: R11 alone +0.175 A, kelvin_check's 1 % taps +0.052 A, C-1's full taps -0.109 A
   R11 alone holds, with kelvin_check's taps holds, with C-1's full 0.38 mOhm FAILS. L4-E4's tap rule at 5.095 A gives 0.2091 mOhm at 25 C
   (C-1's accepted criterion 0.2900 mOhm: NOT met).
   What would change: nothing, if the pin's error at 10 mOhm is at most 0.071 A in that band (bench V-A07); otherwise, by
   L4-E4's own rule, R11 7.0 mOhm (C2904239): C-1 0.9921 mOhm at 25 C, its highest permitted current 8.300 A against 8 mOhm's 7.262 A,
   carried to item 4 (fault handling).
   For comparison, (a) as written: 6.20 A at 36 V, 6.522 A through R11, worst margin -1.252 A with R11 alone; the largest catalogue R11 that would coordinate: 6.0 mOhm

END. Desk arithmetic; nothing is measured. The hardware line and the raised ceiling are not drawn (OWED); the transient
behaviour of every candidate is INCONCLUSIVE until the bench rows of L4E5-SOURCE-CONTROL.md are run.
